# Requirements Authoring Rules

When working in the requirements directory, follow these rules:

## Format Requirements
- Use YAML format exclusively for requirements documents
- Follow the schema in `docs/requirements/requirements-template.yaml`
- Each requirement MUST have a unique ID: `REQ-XXXX` (4 digits, zero-padded)

## Requirement Quality Checklist
- [ ] Uses "shall" for mandatory behavior
- [ ] Is testable with measurable criteria
- [ ] Avoids ambiguous words (fast, robust, user-friendly) unless quantified
- [ ] One idea per requirement (no conjunctions creating compound requirements)
- [ ] Includes rationale explaining why this requirement exists
- [ ] Specifies verification method: Test | Analysis | Inspection | Demonstration
- [ ] Has priority: Must | Should | Could

## Required Fields
```yaml
- id: "REQ-XXXX"
  title: "<short descriptive title>"
  statement: "The system shall ..."
  rationale: "<business/technical justification>"
  verification_method: "Test"
  priority: "Must"
  derived_from: []  # UC-xxxx, PRD references
  notes: ""
```

## After Creating/Editing Requirements
1. Run: `python tools/traceability/check_traceability.py --docs docs --tests tests`
2. Ensure a corresponding design doc will reference this requirement
3. Ensure test cases will be written to verify this requirement

## Related Agents
- Use `agents/requirements-author.md` for creating new requirements
- Use `agents/requirements-reviewer.md` for reviewing requirements quality
